{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And I will bring out My hosts.</b> Scripture called Israel 'My hosts' because they correspond to the host of the spheres — twelve tribes corresponding to twelve signs of the zodiac — and further because they are likened to stars, as it says (Deuteronomy 1:10): ״והנכם היום ככוכבי השמים לרוב״. And further, צבאותי alludes to the supernal host, and the sense of the verse is: 'and I will bring out My hosts' from above together with My people the children of Israel below. This is what they said: the Shekhinah went into exile with them, and if the Shekhinah stood in exile, how much more so [for] the rest of the supernal beings. And this is what they said, RZZ: צבאות is a holy Name and is not erased, because it is called צבאות only on account of the princes of the supernal hosts — and this is what is written (Exodus 12:41): ״יצאו כל צבאות ה׳״, that is to say, the supernal ones and the lower ones."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:40.078458621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}